{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_0187uVyFefMZFhKcBWsfVqpQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All tasks complete. Here's a summary of what was implemented:\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\n### Files Created/Modified\n\n**cmd/ls/main.go** — Full ls implementation with core infrastructure plus extended flags:\n\n- **-i flag** (prd010-ls-extended R3.1): Prepends right-aligned inode number (`sys.FileInfo.Ino`) to each entry in all output formats. Column width computed from the maximum inode number width across all listed entries.\n\n- **-s flag** (prd010-ls-extended R3.2, R3.3): Prepends right-aligned 1K block count (`fi.Blocks/2`) to each entry. Total line printed in all modes (single-col, multi-col, long format). When combined with `-h`, uses the inline binary `humanSize` algorithm per R6.5.\n\n- **-n flag** (prd010-ls-extended R3.4, R6.1): Implies `-l` (long format). Displays numeric UID/GID via `strconv.FormatUint` without calling `os/user.LookupId`/`LookupGroupId`. Per R3.5, when `-i` and `-s` are both active, inode is printed first, then block count, then the entry.\n\n- **-F flag** (prd010-ls-extended R4.1, R4.2, R4.3): Appends type indicators: `/` (directory), `*` (executable, `mode&0o111 != 0`), `@` (symlink), `|` (pipe), `=` (socket). Indicator printed after ANSI reset sequence so it is not colorized.\n\n**cmd/ls/ls_test.go** — Differential test cases for `-1i`, `-1s`, `-ls`, `-n`, `-1F`, `-1is`, `-lF`, `-ni` against gls reference binary.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria Verification\n\n| Criterion | Status |\n|-----------|--------|\n| AC1: `-1i` inode display | Verified manually |\n| AC2: `-1s`/`-ls` block display with total | Verified manually |\n| AC3: `-n` numeric UID/GID | Verified manually |\n| AC4: `-1F` type indicators | Verified manually |\n| AC5: golangci-lint clean | Verified — 0 issues |"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":32